body:
@DemiusAcademius any chance you could put together a simple reproducer (preferably using H2 as the database)?

Thanks!

/cc @FroMage

@DemiusAcademius I tried to reproduce the issue, using Oracle Database, on a close example and I can see my database updated.

I created a Person entity extending PanacheEntity:
```java
@Entity
public class Person extends PanacheEntity {
    public String name;

    public static List<Person> loadEverybody() {
        return findAll().withLock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_WRITE).list();
    }
}
```

I created an endpoint that try to mimic what you implemented (using a query with lock, then findById on the entity, update it, persist it):
```java
@Path("/persons")
@Produces(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
@Consumes(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
public class ExampleResource {

    @GET
    public List<Person> list() {
        return Person.listAll();
    }

    @GET
    @Path("/{id")
    public Person list(@PathParam("id") Long id) {
        return Person.findById(id);
    }

    @POST
    @Transactional
    public void create(Person person) {
        person.persist();
    }

    @GET
    @Path("update-names")
    @Transactional
    public void updateAllName() {
        List<Person> persons = Person.loadEverybody();
        for(Person person : persons) {
            Person toUpdate = Person.findById(person.id);
            toUpdate.name = "John Doe";
            toUpdate.persist();
        }
    }
}
```

But I cannot reproducer the error. If you can give us a reproduer, even on Oracle Database I could have a look at it.
